    "source": "1810 and 1820 census interpolated to 1816, free adult men outside the Southern states; the census gives free white males in bands (16\u201326, 26\u201345, 45+), so men 21+ are split from the 16\u201326 band. Voters were men meeting each state's rules: many states still required property or taxpaying qualifications (Virginia and Rhode Island a freehold). Electors were chosen by popular vote in 10 states; elsewhere (Connecticut, Delaware, Georgia, Indiana, Louisiana, Massachusetts, New York, South Carolina and Vermont) men cast no presidential vote. Free Black men could vote in some Northern states on the same or stricter terms."
   },
   {
