    "source": "1810 and 1820 census interpolated to 1816, white adults in Virginia, North Carolina, South Carolina, Georgia, Tennessee and Louisiana; only men meeting their state's property or taxpaying rules could vote (Virginia required a freehold). The South Carolina, Georgia and Louisiana legislatures chose their electors, so people there cast no presidential vote."
   },
   {
    "key": "black-south",
